# TBD-207 — what HCP Terraform must NOT pack into a configuration version.
#
# The TFC workspace is VCS-driven, so real runs are built from the GitHub
# repository. A LOCAL `terraform plan` is different: it uploads a slug of this
# whole repo for a speculative run, and without this file that upload fails
# outright with:
#
#   illegal slug error: invalid symlink ("frontend/node_modules") has external target
#
# node_modules can hold symlinks that point outside the slug, and the packer
# refuses any such symlink. The practical effect was that nobody could
# run a speculative plan locally at all -- every change had to be validated by
# merging it. Everything below is either unpackable or simply irrelevant to
# infra/terraform.
.git/
.github/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/
backend/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.log
.DS_Store
